WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.377
One of the main benefits of a class is that the same class can create many objects.

00:00:05.377 --> 00:00:07.602
Think about a Product class.

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:13.222
The class can describe what every product should have, such as a name and a price.

00:00:13.222 --> 00:00:16.232
But each object can store different values.

00:00:16.232 --> 00:00:19.882
One object might be a laptop with a price of 900.

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:23.877
Another object might be a monitor with a price of 300.

00:00:23.877 --> 00:00:28.587
Both objects come from the same class, but they are separate objects.

00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:32.392
Changing one object does not automatically change the other.

00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:39.067
This is useful in analytics when we need to represent repeated things with the same structure.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:42.127
For example, customers, products, student scores, sales records,

00:00:42.127 --> 00:00:47.242
or reports could all be represented with classes in some projects.

00:00:47.242 --> 00:00:51.307
The key idea is that a class gives us a reusable blueprint.

00:00:51.307 --> 00:00:55.360
Objects are the actual working examples created from that blueprint.
